    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A rural feel coupled with ultimate convenience, welcome to Hollywoodrath Crescent. Tucked away in this virtually traffic free cul de sac and overlooking a large communal green, No.47 enjoys a quiet and peaceful postioning in this ever popular and cleverly desgined development. \r\n\r\nAccessible from both the N2 and N3, Hollywoodrath Crescent is a mere 13km west of Dublin City Centre and only 14km from Dublin Airport.  The ever expanding range of retail outlets, restaurants and entertainment venues of Blanchardstown Town Centre and Retail Park are just 4.5km from the front door.\r\n\r\nFor those with a family, the development has a playground onsite and also a Nursery & Montessori (Once Upon A Time), both a short 7 minute walk away. Other schools in the neighbourhood incldue St Lukes National School, Tyrellstown Educate Together and Le Cheile Secondary School.\r\n\r\nTo the front of the house there is off street parking for two cars with the added benefit of an EV charge point. A pedestrian side gate leads to the very large rear garden. Designed with low maintenance in mind, it has been landscaped and finished with a paved patio and artifical lawn.  A block built garden room has an electrical supply and could be used as a home gym or office area.\r\n\r\nWith such an abundance of facilites, services and amenities within easy and convenient reach it is clear to see why Hollywoodrath has become such an established and popular development for those seeking a spacious, energy efficient family home. Early viewing is strongly reccommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Passing through the front door leads into the bright reception hall off which is a guest wc and useful under stair storage. To the front of the house overlooking the driveway and communal green beyond, is the main reception room. This has been fitted with extensive built in drawer and shelf storage. To the rear of the house is the very large open plan kitchen and dining room. Overlooking the garden, this light filled space is truly the heart of the home. The kitchen features excellent floor and wall mounted press units which are complemented by marble effect worktops. The seperate utility room has additional built in storage. Floor to ceiling windows in the kitchen / dining room overlook the rear garden.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor there is a family bathroom and four bedrooms. The master bedroom to the front has a walk in wardrobe area and an ensuite shower room."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Reception Hall - \r\nwith a guest wc and separate under stair storage.\r\n\r\nReception Room - \r\nbox bay window, fitted media unit with storage drawers and an integrated fire.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining Room - \r\nspacious room overlooking the rear garden. Floor and wall mounted units with marble effect worktops and integrated appliances.\r\n\r\nUtility Room - \r\nstorage units and plumbing for utilities.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom - \r\ngenerous double room overlooking the communal green. Walk in wardrobe, ensuite shower room.\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\ndouble room to the rear with built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\ndouble room to the rear with built in wardrobes,\r\n\r\nBedroom - \r\nto the front, with built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious semi detached BER A3 rated home.\r\nOff street parking for 2 cars, EV charge point installed.\r\nLarge rear garden with a fully paved patio and an additional deck area.\r\nBlock built garden store with electrical supply.\r\nGenerously proportioned accomodation throughout, ideal for a large family.\r\nClose to all essiential amenities.\r\nConstructed 2017, gas fired central heating."
      },
      {
